    {
      "id": 236007,
      "name": "Sonvar",
      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-03-15T11:38:07.383Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It’s hard to hit everything and zombies are typically alt universe stuff in comics.</p>\n<p>As for what to use, I’d probably suggest that for each Zombie minion hitting a particular target they get +1 to attack as a swarm type thing.  So three zombies hitting one hero would each get +3 to their attack actions.   For a LT zombie, maybe something add on an ability that they cause a hinder based off the roll.</p>\n<p>A heal/resurrect seems more fitting to give as an ability to the villain and not directly to the minions/LTs.   Typically zombies aren’t resurrecting themselves but it’s done by someone else.   They don’t seem to heal that I’ve seen in media either.  At best they might be satiated had they eaten recently but still keep the damage they have on them.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-03-15T14:07:06.405Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 44,
      "readers_count": 43,
      "score": 78.8,
